 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. How are you? It depends how you use them. They can save you time planning and organizing the big day, but they charge for that. Then they' be worth it for the planning gift from the couple. You can do the selling and they' do the hard work. The typical package is a year, so that all parties are welcomed on time. You can say you'll do the selling and they' do the rest for one day salary. It' worth trying at least. Wedding planners are worth it if there's someone with her. Then don't tell her. Give the couple the sales pitch and let them decide. That's the planner's secret weapon. Offer it to the couple privately and see what happens.",
